/**
 * The logo of each programme of the catalogue.
 *
 * Each path fills a box of 24 x 24 with one colour. The longer side of the
 * logo touches the box, and the shorter side stays at the centre. Thus each
 * logo holds the same box and the same format, and `currentColor` gives the
 * colour of the theme. Paragraph 5.7 of `docs/architecture.md` gives the rules.
 *
 * Three sources supply the logos. The comment above each logo gives its
 * source:
 *
 * - Simple Icons, with the licence CC0 1.0. The path is the path of the icon,
 *   with no change.
 * - Wikimedia Commons, for a programme that Simple Icons does not hold. Each
 *   file there is in the public domain as a text logo. A script draws the file,
 *   keeps the part that the comment names, traces it with `potrace` and puts it
 *   in the box. The official sites of these airlines refuse the session of the
 *   harness. Refer to the rule 5 of the data in `CLAUDE.md`.
 * - The official file of the programme, for Flying Blue. Neither Simple Icons
 *   nor Wikimedia Commons holds it. The user gave the address. The same script
 *   traces it.
 *
 * Each logo is a trademark of its owner. The foot of each surface says it.
 */
export type ProgramLogo = { title: string; path: string };

/**
 * The logos, in the order of the catalogue: the three sources first, then the
 * airline programmes. The public page shows them in this order.
 *
 * The key is the `id` of the programme in `src/server/db/seed/catalogue.ts`.
 * The field `title` is the name of the brand of the logo, not the short name
 * of the programme: the logo of `amex-mr` is the logo of American Express.
 */
